[Music]  a few days before continuing my journey  from india to iran  i went to a company of trade ships in  the british raj's office i asked for a  fine room in the ship  and the head of the company said choose  whatever room you want  except for you there's no other sailor  in first class  some days after coming to the ship i  realized i was indeed the only traveller  on this ship  and i could go anywhere i wanted nobody  wanted to travel on the oman sea  and besides there was no one that could  accept the danger of travelling in this  season  on the persian gulf even the true  sailors can barely protect themselves  against such waves  there are a bunch of flies in the ship's  rooms too which annoy everyone on the  ship  the weather is constantly wet and i'm  struggling to barely breathe  the ship's name is ashore  on the 20th of january our ship left  muscat  and despite the pleasing and peaceful  atmosphere of the night  the heat was still galling at midnight  the thermometer was still showing  39 degrees but long last we passed  through the hormos strait  the persian gulf is a historical sea  i remembered that in 325 bc  niacious alexander's admiral sailed from  the mouth of the sinned to the mouth of  the tigris  after this the greeks and romans and  iranians fought against people of barsu  for ownership of the sea after that the  arabs and the portuguese fought  after that dutch but victory was for  britain  the english men in the early 19th  century and they cleared this sea from  the omani pirates  on the 24th of january we arrived to  boucher  the coastal city of boucher now is in  chaos  the iranian government tried with the  help of the englishmen to implement  strict lockdown regulations  but the people closed the bazaar and in  mosques  gathered to rebel  in these kind of journeys people can see  special phenomena which are specific  to certain lands i read before about  this in books but now i'm seeing it with  my own eyes  there was water of a lake in the  distance so calm  and i could clearly see trees i looked  on the map of iran but there wasn't any  lake in that place  so i asked my servant and he answered  there is no lake  that was a mirage  there is a problem with the soldiers in  shiraz not only the riflemen are not  reliable or responsible and cannot  protect anyone  but they regularly ask for gratuity with  such behavior and lack of discipline  i can't use the venerable word soldier  for them  i think nobility responsibility loyalty  to the emperor patriotism gratitude to  serve the country  lack of corruption and ignoring wealth  are virtues which make  japanese soldiers and gunners different  from other countries  one of the most incredible things in  iran is the shu  which is comfortable and durable at the  same time  there are layers in place of toes and  the heel of the shoe is sewn  and then there is a hard insole under it  they call  give the japanese shoe is made of cotton  and in a five-day journey such as this  one  would be destroyed easily  [Music]  there are two ways to travel in iran  caravan  and chaparr on a caravan journey the  traveller has a tent bed and  the other things necessary for travel so  a caravan is significantly easier  and comfortable in comparison to the  chaparra but a traveler has to spend  more money  and time to travel travellers by caravan  can wait and  stay wherever they want for example  along a river and give water to horses  or freely stand upon persepolis  and passer guard to imagine the royal  and noble lives of the great heroes of  history  such as kurosh daryush and  kashaya shah this is the travel way  of a daimyo  on the other hand there is the chapa or  speedy  which i chose this way of travel is hard  and painful just like hikiaku men  on the 20th of august we arrived at a  hillside  and finally could see persepolis  the site was small the columns were like  wooden flag sticks  in local matsuris the column heads of  the halls  stair carvings cornices freezes tombs of  the emperors  no description of such majesty could do  no justice to it  this was the remains of a grand palace  that held the destructive thunder of  alexander  eventually we turned right and saw in  the distance a little  fuji between four other mountains during  this entire trip i saw  nothing natural to compare to the glory  of damavand  that seemed like a second fuji  the sun was setting and the sky was in  twilight  seeing this view in the vast plain was  unbelievable  why didn't i bring my camera  izadcast is one of the strangest places  in the world that people live  the town is on a lone mountain in the  heart of a plane  there is only one way to the town the  muddy houses have  floors and it seems that they're all in  one stronghold  it's like the hanging gardens of babylon  [Music]  on the 14th of september i met atabag  azam amin al-sultan  his imperial highness gladly and  hopefully wished for friendly trade  between our two sublime countries and  subjects  he asked how was the general fukushima  yasumasa  who met him three years ago the power of  the  shah is absolute and he is the owner of  all life and wealth  he is the main statesman of iran and if  i remember correctly he is 47.  how young to be dealing with all the  politics and administer the realm  though his hair was white he appeared a  wise and reasonable man but his  body was weak and tired the great  ambassador of britain  said the shah doesn't really rule at all  the real law  is religious law and the true power is  with the imams  the people of iran do not let foreigners  see their way of life and family  traditions  i only saw half of the people of iran  upper and lower class women cannot meet  with strangers  i heard by the law men can have four  wives and over  and that it depends how wealthy they are  if they can have unofficial and  temporary wives wives are always in the  house with the husbands and can only  speak with female guests  i wonder how iranian women pass their  time and what is their joy in life  iranian food is delicious the main foods  are made from meat  bread vegetable and fruit and recently  they started drinking whiskey  and champagne along with beer which is  deemed a  symbol of modernism they love to hunt  ride and shoot  in recent years people have travelled  from tehran to kasvin  by and there aren't chaparras anymore  so inevitably despite how expensive it  was i chose toroshke  because i had to to arrive in asia minor  we rode day and night because the horse  wasn't a great walker  and multiple times the rider waited and  whipped the horse or  pushed the doroshke to force the poor  horse to move  the road was even worse than the road to  tehran and it didn't even have  one natural wonder recently a private  russian transport company made a new  road for the duroshk  which is still under construction and it  seems there was a collusion between the  two  because i was in a hurry i ended up  paying double at least  i stayed in the hotel kazvin which  belongs to the cosby government  when i awoke the next morning i saw a  rusty old doroshke  but i didn't complain yet after just two  british miles the  roche k broke it was the first time i  saw a vehicle in iran break  the rider went back to kazvin to fetch  another doroshke  so i sent my servant with him and stayed  in the road alone with all my  possessions  the dust blew in my eyes and the sun was  shining in the clear blue  sky passing travellers who saw me on the  road  a foreigner alone with all my things  laughed  and humiliated me and the new doroske  wasn't any good either  it was like the entire carriage between  kiyobashi road to asukasa  every minute on it was agony  [Music]  according to the travel contract i  should pay after arriving at rasht  but the rider stopped before the albors  mountains  and said he wanted his money now and  more  well i'm sure my servant would have  protected me but the heat was growing  and the rider had a gun with him so i  agreed  again in the mist on the mountains one  of the horses with all of my clothes and  some other stuff was lost  but after that the road was glorious and  lovely  and the further we went the greener it  became  there was a steamship in the anzali port  and on the other  side were the persian realms of the  russian empire  and after that i'll finally arrive at  the ottoman empire  my time in iran had been a test of my  patience  both physically and mentally and  immediately  i fell fast asleep on the deck like a  dead man  you

